<Notebook title="Safety · Sparrow Notes" description="Non-negotiable bench and pack rules for Sparrow.">
  <article class="note">
    <div class="stamp">do not skip</div>
    <h1>Safety</h1>
    <p class="frozen">Props are sharp. Packs can fire. Fingers stay outside the disc.</p>
    <div class="wobble warn">
      If a rule on this page fights a later idea, this page wins.
    </div>
    <h2>Bench</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Props off until the arming castle is proven on the bench with no blades.</li>
      <li>DShot 0 is the only disarmed command. Do not “idle” a disarmed bird.</li>
      <li>Never cut motors in the air to save a crash. Fly it down or pancake with spin.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Packs</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Charge the 3S 650 mAh LiPo in a fire bag, on a hard surface, attended.</li>
      <li>LVC warns at 10.5 V and cuts at 9.9 V. A cut latches. Land. Swap.</li>
      <li>A swollen, dropped, or mystery pack is trash, not a flight battery.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>First flights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Indoors or a cage first. Full rings stay on.</li>
      <li>One pack, one person on the radio, one person as a spotter.</li>
      <li>If the estimator dumps attitude, disarm on the ground only.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Notebook>
